// The constraint list's closing bracket.
//
// Deliberately not skip_to_close with the character as a parameter: the two
// differ by a literal, and a literal is exactly what the function-uniqueness
// rule counts as a real difference, so they are two functions rather than one
// parameterised one. Making it a parameter would also mean every caller
// spelling `")"` at the call site, which is less readable, not more.

skip_to_rbrack(int[] pos) {
  while(cur_text(pos) != "]" && cur_kind(pos) != "eof") {
    advance(pos);
  }
} return void;
